  "summary_plain": "Thirty-two printed bars in 2/4: six on each of systems 1 through 4 and eight on system 5. Every bar is a complete bar of two quarter-note beats. There is no pickup and no repeat, and every system ends with a barline through both staves, so no bar is split by a system break. The piece opens with treble over bass and one sharp. P008 ends at a thin-thick double bar, and P009 prints four sharps on each staff. The upper staff changes to bass after the first quarter chord of P011, then prints a cautionary treble before the barline of P012, which governs P013. It changes to bass again after the first quarter chord of P015, and prints a cautionary treble before the barline of P018, which governs P019. The lower staff stays in bass. P016 ends at a thin-thick double bar and the four sharps continue. P024 ends at a double bar with two courtesy sharps on each staff, and P025 prints one sharp on each staff. P031 holds half-note chords with fermatas and still fills two quarter-note beats. P032 fills two quarter-note beats and closes with the thin-and-thick final barline. Red crop rectangles cover both pages, and slurs, hairpins, dynamics, and the final barline stay inside the crops. This reading used only the request, the print, and the proposed frame.",
